WEBVTT

00:40.040 --> 00:40.874
Mrs. Oh!

00:43.543 --> 00:44.627
Are you all right?

00:45.545 --> 00:47.172
It's the coldest day of the year.

00:47.922 --> 00:49.257
Are you able to stand?

00:50.383 --> 00:53.136
Let's go. I'll take you home right now.

00:53.636 --> 00:54.846
Goodness, thank you.

01:11.780 --> 01:13.114
Let me take that.

01:19.204 --> 01:20.205
I'm sorry.

01:21.039 --> 01:24.250
I owe you another one.

01:24.334 --> 01:28.588
Please keep the promise we made.
You agreed to take a break every hour.

01:28.671 --> 01:32.383
I'd like to, but it's not easy.

01:33.468 --> 01:36.387
I need to keep fighting.

01:36.471 --> 01:39.766
- So others'--
- So you can keep others' children safe.

01:39.849 --> 01:43.895
Because the world won't change
unless you do something, right?

01:45.647 --> 01:47.065
I understand how you feel,

01:48.650 --> 01:50.693
but your health comes first.

01:51.194 --> 01:52.362
Goodness.

01:53.863 --> 01:58.618
You're the only person
who understands and cares about me.

01:59.285 --> 02:02.163
Just doing my job.
Go on in and get some rest.

02:02.247 --> 02:03.081
All right.

02:03.581 --> 02:05.625
Hold on. Just one moment.

02:05.708 --> 02:07.794
Wait here for just a moment.

02:15.468 --> 02:21.015
I just made this kimchi,
and it turned out great. Take some.

02:21.099 --> 02:23.434
It's okay, Mrs. Oh.
I'm eating really well.

02:23.518 --> 02:27.230
Come on, you said you love my side dishes.

02:28.356 --> 02:30.483
- I'm really okay, Mrs. Oh.
- Please.

02:31.943 --> 02:36.197
I'm giving this to you
because you remind me of my son,

02:36.281 --> 02:37.282
so just take it.

02:40.827 --> 02:41.828
Thank you.

02:44.247 --> 02:45.290
Get some rest.

03:11.649 --> 03:13.610
Mrs. Oh, we're here. You'll be all right.

03:14.527 --> 03:17.488
You need to stay awake, okay?
Can you hear me?

03:18.823 --> 03:22.160
Only authorized personnel may enter.
Please wait outside.

03:29.834 --> 03:31.085
Is she gonna be okay?

03:40.094 --> 03:42.639
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

03:42.722 --> 03:46.017
Where are you going?
I asked where you were going!

04:05.119 --> 04:06.871
"Police In Name Only" is coming in.

04:11.542 --> 04:12.502
What the hell?

04:13.002 --> 04:14.254
The bastard is back.

04:20.009 --> 04:21.594
I warned you, didn't I?

04:21.678 --> 04:25.473
Has this cop bastard
completely lost his mind?

04:27.350 --> 04:28.685
Where is Gong Seok-ho?

04:53.334 --> 04:54.585
What's all this?

04:55.712 --> 04:57.672
LEE DO

04:58.923 --> 05:01.426
Where are you? What's going on here?

05:01.509 --> 05:04.679
Pat them down
and check if they have an address list.

05:04.762 --> 05:05.972
An address list?

05:06.055 --> 05:08.599
Guys, search all these bastards' pockets.

05:08.683 --> 05:09.517
Hold him down.

05:09.600 --> 05:11.060
What? Hold me down? Fuck you!

05:11.144 --> 05:12.812
Stay still, you dirtbag.

05:12.895 --> 05:15.982
Fuck off, you son of a bitch.
Don't fucking touch me.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.445
You fucking bastards.

05:20.528 --> 05:22.739
Fuck this shit! That fucking hurts.

05:25.241 --> 05:26.075
What is this?

05:26.826 --> 05:27.660
Do!

05:28.244 --> 05:30.079
Did you check the car in that alley?

05:30.163 --> 05:31.831
No, there's no camera over there.

05:31.914 --> 05:34.917
So I was checking
if any nearby cameras caught anything.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.085
And the address list?

05:39.714 --> 05:41.299
What exactly is this address list?

05:51.726 --> 05:52.727
Compare them.

05:56.856 --> 05:58.941
"5 Domyeong-ro 1-gil."

05:59.609 --> 06:00.943
"Oh Kyeong-suk."

06:01.819 --> 06:02.653
What is this?

06:03.863 --> 06:05.490
This is the same address.

06:06.074 --> 06:06.908
That's right.

06:07.658 --> 06:11.204
I don't think the recent shootings
were the work of individuals.

06:11.287 --> 06:12.580
Then what were they?

06:15.208 --> 06:16.542
An organized crime.

06:17.335 --> 06:21.714
The gun deliveries imply someone
is exploiting these people's situations,

06:21.798 --> 06:24.092
hoping they will pull the trigger.

06:24.675 --> 06:26.803
The perpetrators
of this series of shootings

06:26.886 --> 06:29.972
were not people with jobs
that allowed easy access to guns

06:30.056 --> 06:32.725
or the financial resources
to smuggle them.

06:32.809 --> 06:34.435
They were just ordinary citizens.

06:34.519 --> 06:35.436
YEONGSEONG GOSIWON

06:35.520 --> 06:37.939
I suspect that the delivery
of these guns indicates

06:38.022 --> 06:41.526
that a person or an organization
is exploiting their situations,

06:41.609 --> 06:43.194
hoping they will pull the trigger.

06:43.277 --> 06:46.781
The address list before you
is evidence of that.

06:48.533 --> 06:51.828
So each of these boxes
contained a gun and an address list?

06:58.584 --> 07:00.503
Why did they put this in?
For what purpose?

07:01.087 --> 07:04.382
To expose those who received
the address list to each other

07:05.049 --> 07:07.385
because it may cause anxiety.

07:08.010 --> 07:11.013
This means the recipient knows
where more guns are,

07:11.514 --> 07:14.600
while someone else knows they have one.

07:15.476 --> 07:17.270
You remember what Yu said, don't you?

07:17.353 --> 07:18.354
There are

07:19.689 --> 07:20.523
more guns.

07:21.274 --> 07:23.192
There are more people with guns.

07:24.193 --> 07:26.988
Someone might come to you
looking for a gun,

07:27.071 --> 07:28.406
or if you need more guns--

07:28.489 --> 07:30.116
Go find them for yourself?

07:30.199 --> 07:34.495
That's right. Jo U-tae came here
looking for a gun after seeing this list.

07:35.538 --> 07:36.372
Hey, lady.

07:37.623 --> 07:39.000
You have a gun, don't you?

07:39.667 --> 07:41.669
They're not just handing out guns.

07:42.170 --> 07:46.340
They could be watching everything
about those who received the guns.

07:46.424 --> 07:50.303
By the way, what's up with the names
on this address list?

07:50.887 --> 07:51.971
Take a look here.

07:52.054 --> 07:54.682
There should be a nickname
from the phone account setup.

07:54.765 --> 07:56.309
They probably used the nickname.

07:56.392 --> 07:58.603
This is all personal information.

07:58.686 --> 08:00.229
How did they get it?

08:00.313 --> 08:03.649
Everyone on that list
likely has malware on their phone.

08:04.275 --> 08:05.318
Yes, that's correct.

08:05.401 --> 08:08.654
Yu, Jeon, and Oh's phones
were all infected with malware,

08:08.738 --> 08:10.615
granting full access to their phones,

08:10.698 --> 08:14.327
including call logs, text messages,
and personal information.

08:15.286 --> 08:16.287
Wait a minute.

08:16.871 --> 08:20.374
But didn't they all say
there were no actual delivery records?

08:21.083 --> 08:24.754
So I think they deliberately disguised it
as a package.

08:26.214 --> 08:28.799
Package deliveries
are a daily routine in Korea,

08:28.883 --> 08:31.302
and people rarely touch
or notice others' packages.

08:31.385 --> 08:34.180
Seriously, who the hell
is behind this crap?

08:34.263 --> 08:35.473
And for what?

08:36.557 --> 08:40.728
If this is true, this is no small matter.
Let's verify the facts first.

08:41.312 --> 08:46.025
Verify these people's real names
and if they match their actual addresses.

08:46.609 --> 08:50.488
Most importantly, make sure
to check for guns and seize any found.

08:50.988 --> 08:52.031
Yes, sir.

08:52.698 --> 08:53.783
Detective Seo.

08:54.367 --> 08:55.201
Yes, sir.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.497
Lee Do found all this out?

08:59.580 --> 09:03.793
Yes, Officer Lee found all this out,
including today's Oh Kyeong-suk case.

09:04.460 --> 09:07.421
He's already suspended.
Tell him not to get into more trouble.

09:07.505 --> 09:08.506
Yes, sir.

09:09.173 --> 09:11.592
Still, we got this lead, thanks to him.

09:11.676 --> 09:13.427
- We should push harder.
- Yes, sir.

09:13.511 --> 09:15.513
- You get what I mean?
- Yes, I understand.

09:16.013 --> 09:17.974
- And tell him he did well.
- Yes, sir.

09:27.525 --> 09:30.069
Officer Lee.
Are you free to talk right now?

09:30.152 --> 09:31.237
Yes, go ahead.

09:32.446 --> 09:35.324
I did some digging on that Moon Baek guy.

09:35.908 --> 09:38.369
Dongwol Industry
is a state-certified arms supplier

09:38.452 --> 09:40.371
that exports weapons for military use.

09:41.247 --> 09:45.751
They have really tight security
and only respond to official letters,

09:45.835 --> 09:48.004
so I just checked a few basics.

09:49.630 --> 09:53.134
He worked there until the end of last year
before resigning.

09:54.010 --> 09:57.388
The reason for his resignation
was terminal cancer.

09:57.471 --> 10:00.224
I heard he had a great rep
among his coworkers.

10:00.725 --> 10:01.559
Is that so?

10:01.642 --> 10:05.354
By the way, how did you end up
getting involved with him?

10:05.438 --> 10:06.856
Well, it's a long story.

10:07.356 --> 10:09.275
Let's keep this between us for now.

10:09.358 --> 10:11.068
Okay, Officer Lee. Will do.

10:22.496 --> 10:23.497
Seriously?

10:23.581 --> 10:28.085
Where the heck have you been?
You can't just leave without telling me!

10:31.297 --> 10:34.925
- You've been here this whole time?
- Of course. Can't you tell?

10:43.309 --> 10:46.103
This doesn't concern you, so why…

10:50.358 --> 10:51.192
Huh?

10:52.276 --> 10:53.277
Who are you?

10:55.613 --> 10:57.114
If you're grateful,

10:57.198 --> 10:58.616
just say thank you.

11:05.915 --> 11:07.625
I just can't figure you out.

11:16.842 --> 11:18.761
If only I had answered the call…

11:22.973 --> 11:23.974
What did…

11:27.103 --> 11:28.437
Mrs. Oh say earlier?

11:30.314 --> 11:31.148
What?

11:33.484 --> 11:34.485
In the car.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.195
I'm impressed.

11:36.904 --> 11:40.116
With everything going on,
you still caught all of that?

11:43.828 --> 11:44.662
She just said,

11:46.455 --> 11:51.210
"I can die without regrets now,
so you don't need to try so hard for me."

11:52.378 --> 11:53.629
That was all.

11:57.174 --> 12:01.512
By the way, why do you treat her
like your mom when she isn't?

12:03.055 --> 12:04.014
Just because.

12:06.600 --> 12:08.519
She treats me like her own son.

12:10.563 --> 12:11.564
I see.

12:13.691 --> 12:16.152
Still, your real mom
might feel hurt to hear that.

12:20.740 --> 12:22.408
She passed away when I was young.

12:23.075 --> 12:25.161
Stay still, you bastard!

12:25.870 --> 12:27.329
You are under arrest for murder.

12:27.413 --> 12:28.456
- Let go!
- Stay still!

12:28.539 --> 12:30.374
You have the right to an attorney.

12:30.458 --> 12:32.293
You have the right to remain silent.

12:35.963 --> 12:36.797
Sorry.

12:38.799 --> 12:41.677
I don't have a mom either,
so I asked out of curiosity.

12:44.555 --> 12:45.973
Did yours pass away too?

12:46.640 --> 12:49.143
I have no idea.
She could be dead or alive.

12:53.606 --> 12:54.857
All I know

12:56.609 --> 12:58.861
is that it snowed heavily…

13:01.280 --> 13:02.698
the day I was abandoned.

13:05.785 --> 13:09.789
PLEASE WRITE DOWN
THE CHILD'S NAME AND DATE OF BIRTH

13:19.924 --> 13:20.925
Excuse me.

13:26.096 --> 13:27.932
Are you putting your baby in there?

13:32.728 --> 13:33.979
Then let me take it.

13:34.480 --> 13:36.398
I take them out of there anyway.

13:36.982 --> 13:37.983
Well…

13:38.651 --> 13:39.735
It's okay.

13:40.903 --> 13:41.904
It's okay.

13:43.072 --> 13:46.075
The baby will be cold
if you put it in there.

13:48.661 --> 13:50.246
Does the baby have a name?

13:52.331 --> 13:53.332
A name?

13:55.167 --> 13:57.044
I wonder if my mom, who abandoned me,

13:58.212 --> 13:59.588
gave me a name.

14:14.395 --> 14:15.771
Is it a boy or a girl?

14:15.855 --> 14:18.274
No clue. Let's bail before we get caught.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.280
Man, a boy is worth much more.

14:35.165 --> 14:38.544
Why not just buy both
if you're already buying?

14:38.627 --> 14:40.754
If you only take one fucking eye,

14:40.838 --> 14:43.382
how am I supposed to sell
a fucking one-eyed freak?

14:43.465 --> 14:47.011
They say they only need one.
In exchange, they promised good money.

14:47.094 --> 14:47.970
What?

14:48.053 --> 14:49.555
They promised good money!

14:50.514 --> 14:51.849
How much are we talking?

14:51.932 --> 14:53.893
One big one. How does that sound?

14:54.393 --> 14:56.478
All right. Just tell me the blood type.

14:56.562 --> 14:57.521
Blood type AB.

14:57.605 --> 14:58.772
Sure, of course!

14:58.856 --> 15:01.317
- Pick a nice fresh one.
- Of course I will.

15:01.400 --> 15:05.446
All right. Let's open the door.

15:05.529 --> 15:08.782
Let's make some money.

15:08.866 --> 15:15.122
Let's see. Blood type AB…

15:18.500 --> 15:19.335
Hey!

15:20.294 --> 15:22.671
Yeah, you. Come out here.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.173
Come on.

15:29.094 --> 15:33.140
What are we drinking tonight? Soju?

15:33.223 --> 15:34.224
Nope.

15:34.308 --> 15:36.602
Then beer? Nope.

15:36.685 --> 15:41.148
Hard liquor.
We're having some hard liquor.

15:41.231 --> 15:44.652
Let's drink some hard liquor. Oh yeah.

15:44.735 --> 15:45.736
Dear me.

15:46.320 --> 15:48.530
Good work today. You get to keep one.

15:50.032 --> 15:52.201
Hey! Let's go grab some hard liquor!

15:54.787 --> 15:56.580
At that moment, I had a feeling…

15:58.415 --> 16:01.669
my life wasn't going to be
a walk in the park.

16:04.046 --> 16:07.633
And that feeling quickly became reality.

16:11.595 --> 16:14.014
After being returned a few times
by adoptive parents,

16:14.848 --> 16:17.309
they finally sent me far away.

16:22.982 --> 16:24.358
- Mom.
- What?

16:25.025 --> 16:27.152
What's so great about me going to the US?

16:27.653 --> 16:29.613
Everything will be better than here.

16:30.906 --> 16:32.032
If you stay here,

16:33.075 --> 16:35.369
your life will end up in the gutter.

16:36.537 --> 16:38.539
The US is the land of opportunity,

16:39.498 --> 16:41.291
so go and make the most of it.

16:42.626 --> 16:46.088
And if you want to be loved,
always wear a smile.

16:48.924 --> 16:52.553
One more thing. I'm not your mom,
so don't remember me as one.

16:53.470 --> 16:54.471
It's burdensome.

16:56.140 --> 16:59.643
"And if you want to be loved,
always wear a smile."

17:02.980 --> 17:04.773
What a fucked-up thing to say.

17:09.528 --> 17:11.697
She called it the land of opportunity…

17:14.158 --> 17:17.911
but it turned out worse than the gutter.
It was a living hell.

17:51.028 --> 17:55.824
My memory is so good
that I can still feel that pain vividly.

18:00.412 --> 18:02.206
Still, don't pity me too much.

18:04.374 --> 18:05.375
Thanks for today.

18:06.335 --> 18:07.336
Go get some rest.

18:08.378 --> 18:09.379
It's fine.

18:10.672 --> 18:13.634
I might not have time,
but I've got plenty of loyalty.

18:14.510 --> 18:15.636
I'll wait with you.

18:29.608 --> 18:30.609
Fuck-gyu.

18:32.361 --> 18:33.362
Fuck-gyu.

18:37.574 --> 18:39.368
Don't ignore me, you little fucker.

18:40.536 --> 18:42.579
You better be waiting at karaoke later.

18:48.252 --> 18:49.419
Why should I?

18:49.503 --> 18:50.420
What?

18:54.258 --> 18:56.760
Goddamn, why is this bastard
acting up again?

18:56.844 --> 18:58.554
I just don't want to go.

19:00.889 --> 19:01.890
Say that again.

19:02.933 --> 19:03.851
You don't want to?

19:04.685 --> 19:05.644
No.

19:06.395 --> 19:07.813
You fucking bitch.

19:09.022 --> 19:10.357
Want me to leak your pics?

19:11.316 --> 19:13.902
- Seong-jun.
- Get to class now, you punks!

19:15.445 --> 19:16.864
Why aren't you going in?

19:16.947 --> 19:18.574
The bell rang. Get moving.

19:26.874 --> 19:28.584
- Hey, get lost.
- Okay.

19:35.299 --> 19:36.175
Hey.

19:37.050 --> 19:38.051
Say that again.

19:39.094 --> 19:40.220
You don't want to?

19:41.555 --> 19:42.973
You don't want to?

19:43.056 --> 19:44.766
Answer me, you fucking bitch.

19:47.394 --> 19:48.312
Okay.

19:48.812 --> 19:49.646
Stop it.

19:55.068 --> 19:56.403
Hi, guys.

19:56.486 --> 19:58.030
Hello.

19:59.489 --> 20:01.116
What page are we on today?

20:01.700 --> 20:02.576
"Stop it"?

20:03.410 --> 20:04.536
Today, we're going to…

20:04.620 --> 20:05.454
Hey.

20:05.996 --> 20:08.248
Since when did you have a choice?

20:08.332 --> 20:11.335
A slave just shuts up
and does as he's told.

20:22.763 --> 20:25.015
Call her a fucking math bitch.

20:27.684 --> 20:29.686
- I don't want to.
- Do it.

20:31.480 --> 20:34.316
Do it.

20:35.442 --> 20:37.569
I said do it, you motherfucker.

20:38.403 --> 20:39.404
Do it.

20:40.656 --> 20:41.657
Do it.

20:45.494 --> 20:47.204
- What the hell?
- Park Gyu-jin.

20:47.746 --> 20:49.623
What is it? What's the matter?

20:52.251 --> 20:53.585
Hey, you son of a bitch.

20:54.586 --> 20:55.587
Stop it.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.924
When I tell you to stop, just stop.

21:00.300 --> 21:01.927
I told you to stop.

21:03.136 --> 21:05.931
Stop it.

21:06.014 --> 21:08.642
Fucking stop! Just stop it.

21:08.725 --> 21:13.063
Stop it, you fucking asshole.
Just stop it!

21:19.778 --> 21:21.280
Fucking shit!

21:23.740 --> 21:26.743
Officer Lee, that motherfucker.

21:28.704 --> 21:29.913
What's all this about?

21:29.997 --> 21:31.623
That's what I want to know.

21:33.875 --> 21:36.503
Who is this guy,
and why is that pig on my ass about him?

21:42.092 --> 21:42.926
This is…

21:44.511 --> 21:46.596
What is it? You know him?

21:46.680 --> 21:48.223
He's Gu Jeong-man's lackey.

21:48.307 --> 21:49.224
What?

21:50.225 --> 21:51.059
Are you sure?

21:51.143 --> 21:52.769
On the day we took care of Mr. Kim,

21:52.853 --> 21:55.272
I saw this guy standing behind him
with my own eyes.

21:55.355 --> 21:56.940
Gong, you motherfucker!

21:57.024 --> 21:59.443
You fucking bastard! Hey!

22:00.402 --> 22:01.486
- Hey!
- Jeong-man!

22:11.330 --> 22:13.790
Gu Jeong-man, that fucking piece of shit.

22:14.624 --> 22:17.336
Dad, can you help me out?

22:18.378 --> 22:20.339
Huh? Why?

22:20.839 --> 22:22.758
Did you get into trouble? What happened?

22:23.759 --> 22:25.677
Can you lend me some money?

22:25.761 --> 22:27.304
What for? What do you need it for?

22:27.387 --> 22:29.181
I'm not saying I won't pay you back.

22:29.931 --> 22:32.309
Is something up with the captain lately?

22:32.392 --> 22:34.853
You'll understand
when you have kids of your own.

22:35.562 --> 22:39.024
Hey, just pretend you don't know
until he brings it up himself.

22:39.566 --> 22:40.400
Yes, sir.

22:41.109 --> 22:42.736
I'm just worried. That's all.

22:42.819 --> 22:44.821
Oh dear. Why are they arguing?

22:44.905 --> 22:46.615
Just move back in, then!

22:47.657 --> 22:49.701
Emergency contact for Oh Kyeong-suk?

22:52.537 --> 22:56.041
The surgery went well,
so there's no need to worry too much.

22:56.541 --> 22:58.460
Could we talk for a moment?

23:03.965 --> 23:07.886
Mrs. Oh Kyeong-suk
had an internal organ infection,

23:07.969 --> 23:11.056
so after surgery,
we put her in a negative-pressure room.

23:11.556 --> 23:13.058
However, her test results…

23:13.141 --> 23:16.061
Thank you, Mrs. Oh Kyeong-suk.

23:16.144 --> 23:18.855
We'll need to manage the infection
for a few more days.

23:20.649 --> 23:24.569
This afternoon, a subway incident occurred

23:24.653 --> 23:28.115
when people, startled by a peddler
selling toy guns, fled,

23:28.198 --> 23:30.534
tripping over one another
and getting injured.

23:30.617 --> 23:32.536
Amid a spate of recent shootings,

23:32.619 --> 23:36.540
passengers mistook
the toy guns for real ones,

23:36.623 --> 23:39.918
instantly throwing
the subway train into chaos.

23:40.001 --> 23:42.963
Funny how quickly
the world can change, huh?

23:45.132 --> 23:47.050
That's how scary guns are.

23:48.385 --> 23:49.386
Guns are scary?

23:50.303 --> 23:51.138
Yeah.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.142
Guns are scary.

23:57.477 --> 24:00.021
A long time ago,
there was a very peaceful village.

24:01.064 --> 24:04.443
One day, a man left a gun
in the town square and vanished.

24:05.902 --> 24:08.196
But before long, the gun vanished,

24:09.030 --> 24:11.491
and the village
began to change dramatically.

24:12.576 --> 24:15.871
As more people were shot
and killed throughout the village,

24:17.080 --> 24:19.875
distrust began to spread
among the villagers.

24:20.834 --> 24:25.255
People started forming massive lines
at the gun store to buy firearms.

24:29.885 --> 24:31.470
A man watching it…

24:35.056 --> 24:36.683
smiled in satisfaction.

24:39.895 --> 24:41.146
Why do you think he smiled?

24:44.399 --> 24:47.152
Perhaps he thought
it turned out the way he intended.

24:48.236 --> 24:51.781
Making them believe guns are justice
and rely on their power.

24:57.037 --> 24:58.038
And those people?

24:58.872 --> 24:59.706
Huh?

25:01.124 --> 25:03.210
The people who received those guns.

25:04.544 --> 25:08.840
To them, a gun could actually represent
both justice and power.

25:09.674 --> 25:12.802
A gun represents
neither justice nor power.

25:13.970 --> 25:16.473
It does nothing
but lead you to self-destruction.

25:18.767 --> 25:21.144
So you should stop searching for guns too.

25:22.103 --> 25:23.897
You said you didn’t have much time.

25:24.648 --> 25:26.399
You should spend it on yourself.

25:33.865 --> 25:35.450
So who is that man?

25:39.412 --> 25:40.664
The man who left the gun.

25:43.708 --> 25:45.126
An Asian with blue eyes.

25:46.127 --> 25:47.337
That's what I heard.

25:55.887 --> 25:57.055
The boys are all here?

25:57.138 --> 25:58.890
Yeah, I checked myself.

26:00.100 --> 26:01.685
Jeong-man!

26:01.768 --> 26:02.936
Hey, wait here.

26:04.187 --> 26:05.188
Damn it.

26:13.446 --> 26:15.949
Shit, when did so many of them show up?

26:17.117 --> 26:18.285
How is U-tae doing?

26:18.368 --> 26:20.495
According to the nurses…

26:23.415 --> 26:25.166
he could be in a wheelchair for life.

26:27.252 --> 26:28.420
Fuck!

26:29.963 --> 26:31.673
I told him not to be reckless.

26:34.676 --> 26:35.802
What about that bastard?

26:36.928 --> 26:39.222
Have you found the pig
who did this to U-tae?

26:40.056 --> 26:40.890
Not yet.

26:41.474 --> 26:42.601
We're still looking.

26:42.684 --> 26:45.228
Damn it. Just wait
and see what happens for now.

26:50.442 --> 26:52.402
No chance of improving with surgery?

26:52.986 --> 26:53.987
I won't do it.

26:56.448 --> 26:58.700
I don't want to feel
any more pain in this life.

27:08.918 --> 27:10.211
Fucking son of a bitch.

27:17.260 --> 27:18.094
Aren't you coming?

27:19.929 --> 27:20.805
Sorry.

27:48.124 --> 27:49.167
Hello, Officer Jang.

27:50.752 --> 27:52.587
I'm at the hospital right now.

27:54.130 --> 27:55.048
I'm heading down.

27:57.175 --> 27:58.259
See you downstairs.

27:59.636 --> 28:01.513
No, I don't need anything right now.

28:02.222 --> 28:03.682
Okay, got it.

28:04.599 --> 28:05.517
Officer Lee.

28:06.017 --> 28:08.019
Let's grab some food before we go.

28:08.645 --> 28:09.646
I'm hungry.

28:11.481 --> 28:12.482
All right.

28:17.612 --> 28:18.446
Excuse me.

28:19.239 --> 28:20.073
Yes?

28:20.824 --> 28:22.617
It's been bothering me for a while.

28:24.285 --> 28:25.954
I think it's your phone.

28:28.164 --> 28:29.165
My apologies.

28:30.917 --> 28:33.712
SEOK-HO

29:03.575 --> 29:05.326
- Hello, Officer Lee.
- You're here.

29:05.410 --> 29:07.579
This is Moon Baek.
And this is Officer Jang.

29:08.580 --> 29:09.873
Hello.

29:10.373 --> 29:11.833
- Let's go.
- Sure.

29:12.751 --> 29:13.585
Good night.

29:14.627 --> 29:16.337
- Take care of yourself.
- Okay.

29:20.759 --> 29:21.968
Bye!

29:44.282 --> 29:46.701
Keep your distance. It'll be too obvious.

29:49.996 --> 29:52.248
Why won't this bastard stop calling me?

29:53.625 --> 29:55.627
- Why isn't he answering?
- No idea.

29:55.710 --> 29:56.711
SEOK-HO

29:56.795 --> 29:59.380
Are you sure it's okay to ignore his call?

30:00.381 --> 30:02.175
That bastard will get more suspicious.

30:04.177 --> 30:06.596
Fucking hell. Talk about shitty timing.

30:08.973 --> 30:09.974
Hey, pipe down.

30:14.020 --> 30:15.605
- Hello, sir.
- For fuck's sake.

30:16.105 --> 30:17.774
Why haven't you answered my calls?

30:18.650 --> 30:21.486
I'm sorry.
A few of my boys got hurt on a job.

30:21.569 --> 30:22.654
Goddamn it.

30:22.737 --> 30:25.198
- My mind's been all over the place.
- Hey.

30:25.824 --> 30:28.034
- Yes?
- Get over here right now.

30:28.701 --> 30:29.536
Sorry?

30:31.246 --> 30:33.581
- Now?
- That's right, you son of a bitch.

30:33.665 --> 30:35.959
Get your ass over here right away.

30:36.042 --> 30:37.043
Understood.

30:39.879 --> 30:40.964
What should we do?

30:43.716 --> 30:44.717
Turn the car around.

33:19.831 --> 33:20.665
Now,

33:22.458 --> 33:23.876
no more problems, right?

33:24.419 --> 33:25.420
Yes, sir.

33:27.213 --> 33:28.506
Just give us the order.

33:29.632 --> 33:32.760
Find people desperate
to get their hands on a gun.

33:33.386 --> 33:34.387
Yes, sir.

33:36.556 --> 33:38.016
And make no mistakes.

33:38.099 --> 33:38.933
Yes, sir.

38:14.750 --> 38:16.127
Bring up the location of the guns.

38:20.047 --> 38:21.007
Look forward to it.

38:23.217 --> 38:25.344
A new world will soon arise.

42:29.672 --> 42:34.677
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
